<!--
  Synthetic C-CDA Vital Signs section. No patient data.

  The narrative table is ordered Vital Sign, Reading, Time Taken, Comments, so
  reading it by position (date, name, value, unit) puts the vital's name in the
  date and its reading in the name. The entries carry every field explicitly:

    vital-display      code with a displayName, PQ in UCUM, a time of day,
                       a target site
    vital-original     code whose originalText references the narrative cell
    vital-text         code with only code/codeSystem; the observation's <text>
                       references the cell that names it
    vital-code-only    nothing but code/codeSystem/codeSystemName names it
    vital-translation  a PQ in a non-UCUM unit: nullFlavor, number and unit in
                       its translation
    vital-organizer    no effectiveTime of its own: the organizer's
    vital-date-only    an effectiveTime with a date and no time
    (no id)            an observation without an id, identified by content
    vital-unnamed      nothing names it: no code, and a <text> that references
                       an empty cell of its own row

  Every observation but vital-code-only references its table row.
-->
